n\n## BasicAuthModule\nNestJS module that provides and exports [BasicAuthGuard](BasicAuthGuard) configured by `forRoot()`.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.module.ts:7  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.module.js:11\n<a name=\"BasicAuthModule.forRoot\"></a>\n\n### BasicAuthModule.forRoot() ⇒ <code>{ module: typeof BasicAuthModule; providers: (typeof BasicAuthGuard \\| { provide: string; useValue: BasicAuthOptions; })[]; exports: (string \\| typeof BasicAuthGuard)[]; }</code>\nProvides and exports `BasicAuthGuard` configured with `options`.\n\n**Kind**: static method of [<code>BasicAuthModule</code>](#BasicAuthModule)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.module.ts:9  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.module.js:13\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795628674043},"tdata:src/basic-auth.guard.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard()","longname":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"constructor","description":"Hashes the configured credentials once; `AUTH_*` pairs are appended when both are set.","memberof":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"order":5,"returns":[{"type":{"names":["BasicAuthGuard"]}}]},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard","longname":"BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"member","scope":"global","description":"HTTP Basic authentication guard (RFC 7617).\n\nCredentials are taken from the first source that has them:\n1. the `Authorization` header, which is authoritative when non-empty\n   (a malformed value is rejected, with no fallback);\n2. the `headerNames` header pair;\n3. `body.auth`, when `body: true`.\n\nRoutes marked `@SkipBasicAuth()` pass without checks. On success `req.user` is\nset to the credentials; on failure a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge is set and a\n401 is thrown.\n\nWorks as `new BasicAuthGuard(options)`, `@UseGuards(BasicAuthGuard)`, or via\n`BasicAuthModule.forRoot(options)`.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":75},"order":3,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:50","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:79"},"level":0},{"id":"BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS","longname":"BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS","name":"BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Injection token for {@link BasicAuthOptions} (provided by `BasicAuthModule.forRoot()`).","meta":{"lineno":46},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:21","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:21"},"level":0},{"id":"digest","longname":"digest","name":"digest","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"SHA-256 digest: fixed length, so `timingSafeEqual` never throws and lengths never leak.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":53},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:28","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:54"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["NonSharedBuffer"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"readHeader","longname":"readHeader","name":"readHeader","kind":"function","scope":"global","description":"Node lowercases header names; only `set-cookie` is ever an array.","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":55},"order":2,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:30","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:57"},"level":0},{"id":"BasicAuthGuard#matches","longname":"BasicAuthGuard#matches","name":"matches","kind":"function","scope":"instance","description":"Constant-time check against every expected pair; both comparisons always run.","memberof":"BasicAuthGuard","params":[],"meta":{"lineno":147},"order":6,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:109","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:151"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["boolean"]}}],"level":0},{"id":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","longname":"<anonymous>~BasicAuthGuard","name":"BasicAuthGuard","kind":"class","scope":"inner","memberof":"<anonymous>","meta":{"lineno":94},"order":4,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/basic-auth.guard.js:56","src":"src/basic-auth.guard.ts:84"}}],"fp":"5294167531ecd117f768661162de0de6b529f96b122bef45a2f00fa5f5762599","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795628673534,"symbols":0},"md:src/basic-auth.guard.ts":{"fp":"59a211cd22a5d8cbb224b595b8760bae6ff10e02623ce91bb19877af11aaa02d","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Members\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#BasicAuthGuard\">BasicAuthGuard</a></dt>\n<dd><p>HTTP Basic authentication guard (RFC 7617).</p>\n<p>Credentials are taken from the first source that has them:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>the <code>Authorization</code> header, which is authoritative when non-empty\n(a malformed value is rejected, with no fallback);</li>\n<li>the <code>headerNames</code> header pair;</li>\n<li><code>body.auth</code>, when <code>body: true</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Routes marked <code>@SkipBasicAuth()</code> pass without checks. On success <code>req.user</code> is\nset to the credentials; on failure a <code>WWW-Authenticate</code> challenge is set and a\n401 is thrown.</p>\n<p>Works as <code>new BasicAuthGuard(options)</code>, <code>@UseGuards(BasicAuthGuard)</code>, or via\n<code>BasicAuthModule.forRoot(options)</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS\">BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Injection token for <a href=\"BasicAuthOptions\">BasicAuthOptions</a> (provided by <code>BasicAuthModule.forRoot()</code>).</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n## Functions\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#digest\">digest()</a> ⇒ <code>NonSharedBuffer</code></dt>\n<dd><p>SHA-256 digest: fixed length, so <code>timingSafeEqual</code> never throws and lengths never leak.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#readHeader\">readHeader()</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Node lowercases header names; only <code>set-cookie</code> is ever an array.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard\"></a>\n\n## BasicAuthGuard\nHTTP Basic authentication guard (RFC 7617).\n\nCredentials are taken from the first source that has them:\n1. the `Authorization` header, which is authoritative when non-empty\n   (a malformed value is rejected, with no fallback);\n2. the `headerNames` header pair;\n3. `body.auth`, when `body: true`.\n\nRoutes marked `@SkipBasicAuth()` pass without checks. On success `req.user` is\nset to the credentials; on failure a `WWW-Authenticate` challenge is set and a\n401 is thrown.\n\nWorks as `new BasicAuthGuard(options)`, `@UseGuards(BasicAuthGuard)`, or via\n`BasicAuthModule.forRoot(options)`.\n\n**Kind**: global variable  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:79  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:50\n<a name=\"BasicAuthGuard+matches\"></a>\n\n### basicAuthGuard.matches() ⇒ <code>boolean</code>\nConstant-time check against every expected pair; both comparisons always run.\n\n**Kind**: instance method of [<code>BasicAuthGuard</code>](#BasicAuthGuard)  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:151  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:109\n<a name=\"BASIC_AUTH_OPTIONS\"></a>\n\n## BASIC\\_AUTH\\_OPTIONS\nInjection token for [BasicAuthOptions](BasicAuthOptions) (provided by `BasicAuthModule.forRoot()`).\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:21  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:21\n<a name=\"digest\"></a>\n\n## digest() ⇒ <code>NonSharedBuffer</code>\nSHA-256 digest: fixed length, so `timingSafeEqual` never throws and lengths never leak.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:54  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:28\n<a name=\"readHeader\"></a>\n\n## readHeader()\nNode lowercases header names; only `set-cookie` is ever an array.\n\n**Kind**: global function  \nsrc: src/basic-auth.guard.ts:57  \ndist: dist/basic-auth.guard.js:30\n","symbols":7,"lastUsed":1795628673749},"tdata:src/schema.ts":{"doclets":[],"fp":"416cb18c5baab346f613da879db006063bddf9b2cc0f728ba25f53885f63846f","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795628673537,"symbols":0},"md:src/schema.ts":{"fp":"27f61b9a87210e6b74add9a7414450678f97e1874b4fd1868910becf67355370","issues":[],"kind":"md","skipped":"no-jsdoc","symbols":0,"lastUsed":1795628673564},"tdata:src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts":{"doclets":[{"id":"SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY","longname":"SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY","name":"SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Metadata key used to mark a route or controller as public.\nSet by {@link SkipBasicAuth} and read by `BasicAuthGuard`.","meta":{"lineno":6},"order":0,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/skip-basic-auth.decorator.js:6","src":"src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts:7"},"level":0},{"id":"SkipBasicAuth","longname":"SkipBasicAuth","name":"SkipBasicAuth","kind":"constant","scope":"global","description":"Marks a route handler or controller as public: `BasicAuthGuard` skips all\nBasic auth checks for it, so no credentials are required and `req.user` is\nleft untouched.\n\nWorks with global guards (`app.useGlobalGuards(new BasicAuthGuard())`),\nper-route guards (`@UseGuards(...)`), and guards provided through\n`BasicAuthModule.forRoot()` — the decorators only need Nest's metadata, not\ndependency injection.\n\nMethod-level metadata takes precedence over class-level metadata, so a\nprotected route inside a public controller can opt back in by setting the\nkey to `false` with `SetMetadata(SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY, false)`.","examples":["```ts\nimport { Controller, Get } from \"@nestjs/common\";\nimport { SkipBasicAuth } from \"nestjs-basic-auth\";"],"customTags":[{"tag":"controller(\"health\")","value":"export class HealthController {"},{"tag":"get()"},{"tag":"skipbasicauth()","value":"check(): string {\n    return \"ok\";\n  }\n}\n```"}],"meta":{"lineno":36},"order":1,"mdaics":{"dist":"dist/skip-basic-auth.decorator.js:36","src":"src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts:38"},"returns":[{"type":{"names":["import(\"@nestjs/common\").CustomDecorator<string>"]}}],"level":0}],"fp":"a9a58a52aadf6688fd1c6505993b565a740e972870c4048117279d520d9faa6f","issues":[],"kind":"tdata","lastUsed":1795628673537,"symbols":0},"md:src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts":{"fp":"dd51ebacdcfa3f3ab925205bb70a258d3de026b17a99a625397b0df67dc0c602","issues":[],"kind":"md","markdown":"## Constants\n\n<dl>\n<dt><a href=\"#SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY\">SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Metadata key used to mark a route or controller as public.\nSet by <a href=\"#SkipBasicAuth\">SkipBasicAuth</a> and read by <code>BasicAuthGuard</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt><a href=\"#SkipBasicAuth\">SkipBasicAuth</a> ⇒ <code>import(&quot;@nestjs/common&quot;).CustomDecorator&lt;string&gt;</code></dt>\n<dd><p>Marks a route handler or controller as public: <code>BasicAuthGuard</code> skips all\nBasic auth checks for it, so no credentials are required and <code>req.user</code> is\nleft untouched.</p>\n<p>Works with global guards (<code>app.useGlobalGuards(new BasicAuthGuard())</code>),\nper-route guards (<code>@UseGuards(...)</code>), and guards provided through\n<code>BasicAuthModule.forRoot()</code> — the decorators only need Nest&#39;s metadata, not\ndependency injection.</p>\n<p>Method-level metadata takes precedence over class-level metadata, so a\nprotected route inside a public controller can opt back in by setting the\nkey to <code>false</code> with <code>SetMetadata(SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY, false)</code>.</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n\n<a name=\"SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY\"></a>\n\n## SKIP\\_BASIC\\_AUTH\\_KEY\nMetadata key used to mark a route or controller as public.\nSet by [SkipBasicAuth](#SkipBasicAuth) and read by `BasicAuthGuard`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \nsrc: src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts:7  \ndist: dist/skip-basic-auth.decorator.js:6\n<a name=\"SkipBasicAuth\"></a>\n\n## SkipBasicAuth ⇒ <code>import(&quot;@nestjs/common&quot;).CustomDecorator&lt;string&gt;</code>\nMarks a route handler or controller as public: `BasicAuthGuard` skips all\nBasic auth checks for it, so no credentials are required and `req.user` is\nleft untouched.\n\nWorks with global guards (`app.useGlobalGuards(new BasicAuthGuard())`),\nper-route guards (`@UseGuards(...)`), and guards provided through\n`BasicAuthModule.forRoot()` — the decorators only need Nest's metadata, not\ndependency injection.\n\nMethod-level metadata takes precedence over class-level metadata, so a\nprotected route inside a public controller can opt back in by setting the\nkey to `false` with `SetMetadata(SKIP_BASIC_AUTH_KEY, false)`.\n\n**Kind**: global constant  \n**Controller(&quot;health&quot;)**: export class HealthController {  \n**Get()**:   \n**Skipbasicauth()**: check(): string {\n    return \"ok\";\n  }\n}\n```  \n**Example**  \n```ts\nimport { Controller, Get } from \"@nestjs/common\";\nimport { SkipBasicAuth } from \"nestjs-basic-auth\";\nsrc: src/skip-basic-auth.decorator.ts:38  \ndist: dist/skip-basic-auth.decorator.js:36\n","symbols":2,"lastUsed":1795628673845}},"version":1}